    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d5c22894-ade2-5633-9469-a3c40864e286",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 44\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -44\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=32 \\\\ y &=-44\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-44$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\left(-44\\right)=32\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=32+44=76.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=76$ and $y=-44.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
