      ":question/id": "6fa89755-eb5f-5aa4-8741-70a203ebe024",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 32 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -40\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=32 \\\\ y &=-40\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-40$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\left(-40\\right)=32\\,\\Rightarrow\\,x=32+40=72.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=72$ and $y=-40.$",
